# Scoped ignores for the _map-analysis/ workspace.
# Keep: source code (.py / .js / .html / .css / .md), the calibration webapp,
#       the 3D render viewer (incl. vendored three.js), the per-map calibration
#       configs (the user's irreplaceable work product), the render manifest,
#       AND the render/data/ extraction outputs (3d JSONs, composite PNGs,
#       and tile textures -- vendored for one-click post-clone review; see
#       the dedicated note further down).
# Skip: anything that's regenerable or third-party content AND that we don't
#       want surfaced in the repo (heavy Steam map dumps, deprecated tools).

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Heavy data / third-party content -- not version-controlled.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------

# Game files copied from a local Steam install.
# Regenerate via `python scripts/ingest_maps.py`.
vsrmaplist/

# Third-party PPM renders from the community ("King's renders").
ppm/

# Vendored third-party tools (bz2terraineditor, BZNTools) -- own LICENSE files,
# pull as git submodules / external clones if needed.
archive/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated artifacts -- regenerable from configs + ingest.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------

# BZN-derived per-map data, refreshed by `python scripts/init_configs.py`.
calibration/map_data/

# Tier-folder overlay PNGs, regenerated by `python scripts/reprocess.py`.
calibration/proven/
calibration/borderline/
calibration/hand_cal/
calibration/failed/
calibration/no_png/

# Production-bound clean overlay PNGs (output stage; same regenerator).
calibration/staging/

# Note: the 3D-render-extract data tree (formerly `_map-analysis/render/data/`)
# was moved to project-root `data/render/` in the 2026-05 render-pipeline
# consolidation. It's still INTENTIONALLY tracked in git so a fresh clone can
# open _map-analysis/render/index.html?map=<stem> without running any
# pipeline first. The tracked artifacts now live under `data/render/`:
#   - data/render/*.3d.json        (per-map heightmap + objects, ~60 MB)
#   - data/render/*.{color,alpha1,alpha2,alpha3}.png  (tier-3 composite
#                                   inputs, ~95 MB)
#   - data/render/tiles/*.dds      (BZ:CC tile textures copied from a local
#                                   Steam install, ~420 MB)
#   - data/render/_manifest.json   (map switcher directory)
#   - data/render/tiles/_manifest.json
# All of these are regenerable via `python scripts/process_stats.py`
# (which transparently runs `build_3d_extracts` -> `extract_3d.extract_one`)
# or by hand via `python scripts/extract_3d.py --all` +
# `python scripts/extract_tile_textures.py` after an `ingest_maps.py` pass.
# We vendor them so the viewer is one-click reviewable post-clone.
# Heads up: the .dds tiles are BZ:CC game assets and are tracked under
# the implicit assumption that this repo's distribution scope tolerates
# that. Strip them back to ignored if that ever changes.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Caches + diagnostic noise.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------

*.log
*.bak
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Throwaway investigation scripts (legacy proof folder under scripts/).
scripts/proof/
